WEBVTT

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:02.080
It's starting!

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:17.460
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.040
Teachers, could you look 
this way for a moment?

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.210
I'm sorry for startling you!

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.290
Yamaguchi-san!

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:46.580
Prize shot!

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.380
An inappropriate 
relationship between

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.780
one homeroom teacher and another.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:53.590
Wait, what? 
What?! What?!

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:54.970
Even if it's an assignment,

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:56.560
you guys still need to be considerate

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.610
of your location and subject.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:02.430
What? Is this for design class?

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:03.330
Yup!

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.670
The assignment is called

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:06.580
"Scene Composition in Photography".

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.340
What do you have to do?

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.910
First, you take a picture of your choice.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:11.240
Here's the one from just now!

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:15.140
Then you attach some 
headline copy and turn it in!

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:18.180
 Big Scoop!!

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:18.180
<b>Staff Room
 Teachers' 
Love Romance?!</b>

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:18.180
Can't you use a different 
photo as an example?

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:21.390
But, Professor, I can't seem 
to take any good photos.

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:22.970
They're out of focus or blurry.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.780
Well that's to be expected 
since you're new at this.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.690
You haven't developed 
a hand for cameras yet.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:29.620
The important thing is how 
you create your composition.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:33.730
Creative composition makes 
for interesting photography.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:34.880
Professor, Professor!

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.330
You mean like these?!

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:39.740
<b> A giant and-        A falling person</b>

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:42.070
<b> L-Leave it to me!</b>

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.070
<b> A giant and-</b>

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:47.080
<b>The Importance of Photography</b>

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.010
Unlike painting,

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.710
I thought photography would be

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.810
quick and easy, but...

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.250
It's more difficult to express your

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:58.090
personality through photography 
than through painting.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.650
I don't have any sense 
for photography either.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.030
Before I even think about the assignment

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.650
I'll have to practice taking pictures.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.040
In some ways,

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.760
these could be said to 
exhibit a certain personality.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:08.810
Lemme see.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:15.240
This isn't a continuous shot?

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.850
Ooh, so then it's the background

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.560
that's being changed rapidly?

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:20.610
I already said I don't have 
an eye for photography!

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:23.210
Well, there's a technique 
that'll help avoid

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:25.330
this kind of composition 
called "The Rule of Thirds."

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.970
It might help if you learned it.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.390
"Division by Thirds"?

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.610
You divide your composition 
into thirds, like this,

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.170
and align to the person or horizon

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.220
on the points where the lines cross.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:38.400
The composition looks less 
amateurish and more interesting.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:42.140
Look, the photo that Masa just 
took is divided into thirds.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.270
The subject is off center

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:45.680
while the overall balance 
feels more stable, right?

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.100
Actually, I meant to 
capture the whole subject.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.380
How did you take that then?!

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.340
All right, I'm going to 
take a bunch of photos

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:57.170
so show me your gravure modeling, Noda! {http://www.gaa.org/what-is-gravure Not sure "gravure" is the right word here. -T}

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:57.780
Okay!

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:00.860
Don't let my cuteness overwhelm 
you and steal your heart!

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:01.830
What're you saying?

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:04.790
It's through my photography that 
you're gonna turn into a beauty.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:06.020
All right, ready?

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.180
Huh? Aren't you going to take any more?

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:28.570
Uh, no... I needed to give 
my eyes and heart a break.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:33.420
Divide the scene into thirds 
and line up the points with...

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.360
I wouldn't get so preoccupied with that.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.790
Although technique is important...

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.160
Huh? But...

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.250
Photography and painting 
are not all that different.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.240
That moment that is held 
inside is expressed

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.650
in whatever way you feel is right.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:52.070
When you paint, Kisaragi-dono,

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:54.170
you have a much softer expression.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:59.140
I feel like you should take 
photographs in the same way.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.310
You're right.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:05.500
Just like when I'm choosing 
a scene to sketch...

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:09.350
I'll express that moment that is held-

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.200
My subjects are running away!

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.360
You two! Don't put the 
chicken lords to work!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.360
What do you think of this?!

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.150
That's amazing, Tomokane!

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.240
You've really improved!

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.120
What's this?

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.870
So you went with that one after all?

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:27.890
Try to keep the pranks 
to a minimum, okay?

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.290
It's not a prank you know.

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:31.300
It's called being too nosy!

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.980
The copy should be 
"Be honest with yourselves!"

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.260
Okay! Finished!

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:36.470
What did you make?

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:39.660
Oh! From the time when we got 
in the way of your photo!

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:42.510
I didn't get to use the "Division 
by Thirds" technique,

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.620
and the ad copy is 
fairly unexceptional,

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:49.070
but I feel like it's a piece 
that is probably my own.

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:49.640
<b> All of us, as always.</b>

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:50.860
<b> Staff Room</b>

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:52.490
Next is...

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.560
This one.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.160
That Noda...

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.520
made another prank 
compositional photograph!

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:09.880
Huh?

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:12.140
You're copying? Class materials?

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.620
Uh, yes. Something like that...

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:18.120
Hey, hey, Kyouju.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.570
What's our schedule for today?

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:23.460
I have it written in my notebook.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:24.360
Thank you.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.730
Kyouju, what's our first class?

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:30.670
Pan...

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:31.530
Pan?

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.000
Design.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.010
<b>1st Period  Design</b>

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:36.970
AIDMA law.

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:38.580
The five stages of 
behavioral psychology

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.480
wherein a consumer is influenced 
into buying a product.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:44.450
Question: What does AIDMA stand for?

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:50.870
AIDMA law.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:52.570
The five stages of behavioral psychology

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:55.480
wherein a consumer is influenced 
into buying a product.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:58.840
Question: What does AIDMA stand for?

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:58.840
I have no idea...

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.000
Ah!

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.000
Do I buy it? What do I do?

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.000
ATM usage is systematic.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:05.870
<b> High Class Oolong Tea</b>

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:07.610
<b> Milk Drink for Children</b>

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:08.570
What are those?

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.610
The concept is "designs that 
reduce consumer interest."

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.480
<b>2nd Period  Coloring</b>

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:16.150
White

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:17.720
Black

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:19.200
Yellow

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.330
Blue-Green

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.220
Purple!

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:22.070
Come on!

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:22.930
Come again?

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.840
I love mixing colors!

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.720
Let me mix! Let me mix!

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.720
What a princess...

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:30.090
Then, could you make 
me a grey like this?

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:31.230
Roger!

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.460
Oops. Too much white.

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:40.740
This time it's too black.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:43.140
Done!

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.010
And yet the color is still wrong.

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:48.010
<b>3rd & 4th Period  Painting</b>

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:48.750
Whoa!

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:50.370
What's that look?

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:51.750
These are work clothes!

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:53.750
Whoa! It's like a doctor's!

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.250
Lemme see! Lemme see!

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:56.780
Take it off! Take it off!

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:57.760
Sure!

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.120
Man, this is sweet. Did you buy it?

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.120
Oh, no.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.330
All incoming students 
should have received one,

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.760
along with your art supplies.

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:07.260
It can even get dirty, it's okay.

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:09.270
<b> Great Painter</b>

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:09.270
Yeah, you're right!

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:13.460
All right! I'm gonna really paint!

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:14.740
I feel so inspired!

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:17.510
Let's see... red... red.

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:22.250
Let me wash, let me wash...

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:25.300
I used too much force and killed it.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:27.690
Who?

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:31.550
Huh? What's this?
 When in the world...?!

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:33.990
It was YOU! NODA!

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:35.990
Wipe your hands!

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:40.230
It suits you, Tomokane-dono.

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:42.460
Wait. You're serious, aren't you?

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:45.270
Then why don't you paint 
whatever you want?!

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.310
You're right. In that case...

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:48.930
Put some red over here.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.900
Then I'll put a dragon in! A dragon!

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.280
Hey, you guys!
 The canvas is over here!

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.280
 And then, Lunchtime

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:56.790
Wait up!

00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:00.160
No box lunches for you three today?

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:00.870
Nope!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:04.600
Yesterday we decided to 
eat at the cafeteria!

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.470
Then, today's lunch will be lively.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:10.780
Usually it's just us, 
so we get to eat in peace.

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:12.030
We thought you'd say that, so...

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:14.970
We brought some entertainment!

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:17.330
We made them during class!

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:19.190
What for?
 We're just eating lunch!

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:21.340
This way we definitely
 won't get bored!

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:24.100
To make sure you don't just 
eat your food in peace!

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:27.430
You thought of this yesterday 
during lunch, didn't you?

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:31.340
Take one!

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.610
All right, All right.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:33.980
Ready, and...

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:35.890
Safe... apparently.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:37.130
Empty lottery?

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:37.860
What?

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:40.610
Trade half of your favorite 
food with someone else?

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:42.220
What'd you get?

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:43.590
Tea service.

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:45.150
Oh, what a relief!

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:46.600
I got "No Sauces."

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:49.060
"No Chopsticks"

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:50.100
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:55.040
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.880
Don't let my cuteness overwhelm you

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:54.290
and steal your heart!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.770
Soy sauce.

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:58.230
Worcestershire Sauce.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:00.330
Salt and pepper.

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:02.490
Chili sauce.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.050
Okay! Let's begin!

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:06.280
Begin what?

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:09.240
But I love pouring sauces!

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.790
I wanna pour! I wanna pour!

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:12.630
Okay, okay. Fine.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.880
What do you want? All of them?

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:15.820
Just the Worcestershire.

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:17.740
Don't use anything else.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.150
Sorry for making you wait!

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:20.330
Kisaragi.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:23.530
Tomokane-san and Kyouju-san 
will be a little while longer.

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:25.800
Yeah, the fried food is 
always popular, so-

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:27.300
Here, Namiko-san!

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:32.340
Kisaragi-chan, would you 
like some sauce, too?

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:34.690
I'm prohibited from using sauce, so...

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:37.020
Oh! I was tea service!

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.190
I'll help.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.160
Let's eat!

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:58.490
Namiko-san, weren't you
 supposed to trade half

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:00.600
of your favorite food with someone else?

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:03.420
Then, I'll trade half my omelet 
with half of your katsudon.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.330
Huh?

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:09.840
I feel like this isn't fair somehow...

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.280
Well it's the rules, so...

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:15.140
Stop! You can't break the rules!

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:15.990
Calm down.

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:19.370
I know. I'm not an idiot.

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:21.530
"Chopsticks" is a homonym for "the edges"

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:21.530
If I can't use the edges,

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.400
I'll use the middle!

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:26.160
What is that!

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:26.870
Oh shoot!

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:27.530
A pun?!

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:29.270
Soup

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:29.270
Clear!

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.140
Omelet

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:31.140
Clear!

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:34.270
Katsudon

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:36.520
Middle, middle...

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:38.300
Tomokane-san.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.270
I brought a spoon,

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:42.010
so please use this instead.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:47.020
It's not coming out.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:50.350
Oh, that button's a little faulty.

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:52.170
Use this one instead.

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:55.000
Oh! Thank you.

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:57.820
That student was a second year,

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.290
judging by his jacket color.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:01.180
As you'd expect from an upperclassman,

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:02.770
they sure are a lot more 
familiar with the school.

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:03.730
Oh, my cell phone.

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:07.760
If you're at the cafeteria 
vending machine,

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:11.300
get me a juice. 
Second row, third from the right. -Uozumi

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:14.040
We're at the cafeteria too,

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.720
so buy us a couple bottles 
of tea. <3 -President

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:19.600
As expected from an upperclassman.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:22.050
Crap. How did they know I was here?!

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.050
Hi-chii-.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:25.300
Shichi.

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:26.430
Hichi.

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:27.730
Shichi.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:28.870
Hi-chi.

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:30.010
Shichi.

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:32.300
What are you doing, Mizubuchi-senpai?

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:35.040
Just teaching my Chubu-dialect friend

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.490
how to pronounce proper Japanese.

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:41.810
Geez! Just give me the hichimi 
seasoning! Hichimi~!

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:43.810
<b>5th & 6th Period  Portraits</b>

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:46.410
My sketchbook is already full!

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:47.810
I only just bought it, too.

00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:50.830
You've been drawing quite a bit.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.180
I'll head over to the supply shop.

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:55.120
Hey, hey. Can I look 
at your sketchbook?

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:55.950
Me too!

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:58.100
Okay, but there are doodles
 and stuff in there, too,

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:00.190
so don't laugh too much!

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:06.700
What happened to you two?

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:10.770
101 cats are on parade!

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:15.470
Thanks for being my model.

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:16.840
What? With Noda?

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:17.980
Oh, how rude!

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:19.540
What about this pose?

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.740
<b> 5 Minutes later</b>

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:20.700
Don't move.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:22.930
Still??

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.700
<b> 20 Minutes later</b>

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:23.850
Quiet.

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:25.630
I'm tired!

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:26.700
<b> 40 Minutes later</b>

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:26.980
That's my line!

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.490
<b>After
 School</b>

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:34.730
I'll take your textbooks as well.

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:35.920
Thanks!

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:41.780
What happened to the 
board that was here?

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:43.870
It was just taken away!

00:13:44.570 --> 00:13:46.690
I was about to make an order...

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:48.700
Do you remember how big it was?

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:52.220
About this big, I think?

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:54.400
All right, I'm getting 
something to measure with.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:55.130
Don't move!

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:56.410
Huh? Like this?

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:03.360
Tomokane-san, hurry up!

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:09.230
Got it.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:16.730
<b>Left behind</b>

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:20.900
Yes, this is reporter Nodamiki.

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:22.880
Behold. These are the ones 
that were left behind.

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:24.610
Left-behind-scenery!

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:29.180
Today takes place in the 
afterschool art room!

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.150
What is she up to now?

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:34.040
Without further ado, let's go 
interview a few GA students.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:35.420
Cameraman, this way.

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:37.630
Yes, you, the slightly out of focus one.

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:38.620
What will you do now?

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:40.320
Um? Um...

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:42.110
I'm making a minimalist piece

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:47.210
for the art assignment
 "modern techniques".

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:47.830
Really.

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:50.930
Now face that camera and 
tell everyone how you feel!

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:52.450
Your mother is watching right now!

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:53.940
Um, my vision is blurry and I can't...

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:54.950
Hey! Hey!

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:57.180
The assignment is due today 
so quit playing around!

00:14:57.810 --> 00:14:59.110
<b> Insert quip/retort here</b>

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:59.110
I don't need cues!!

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.100
Here! Thanks.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:04.640
My eyes are still spinning!

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:06.430
It must be nice for you,

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:08.120
having already turned 
in your assignment.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:11.860
Modern art isn't made from 
hard work but from feeling.

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:14.860
Whether you spend a moment or a day

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:16.260
probably doesn't matter.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:17.490
You would say that.

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:19.430
Noda-chan, what did you submit?

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:22.400
Let's see. It's called "Scratch,"

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:23.570
but can you tell what it is?

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:24.640
Black.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:25.930
No... darkness of night.

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:27.500
Kyuoju's emotional landscape!

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:29.480
Cutting corners.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:31.510
You're all trying too hard.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:34.080
This is a layer coated with crayon.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:37.100
When you scratch it with a pen... See?

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:38.820
The other colors are revealed.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:40.470
This is "Scratch"!

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:43.410
Try it out Kisaragi-chan. 
It's really fun!

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:44.970
Wow! You're right.

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:46.820
As I scratch, the colors 
underneath come-

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.060
<b> Winner!</b>

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:50.870
Winner!

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:51.380
Oh, I don't care anymore.

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:52.290
We have a winner!

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:55.300
Oh, no. I'm out of red.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:57.250
Masa, do you have any red?

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:05.110
Is any red okay?

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:08.050
Yeah, if it's acrylic or water based.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:11.410
In the past, when an artist didn't have

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:13.210
a certain color they would use

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:15.520
pigmentation in flowers and plants.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:19.460
Strawberry jam?!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:22.840
Is this all you had?

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.030
Yes.

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:29.360
Just waiting is boring, too.

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:32.530
Hey Namiko-san, I'm bored! I'm bored!

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:34.570
What a troublesome princess.

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.010
Here.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:38.300
We have plenty of supplies,

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:40.240
so why don't you make 
something on your own?

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:46.590
I'm bored again.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.060
A long, long time ago,

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:51.290
in a place not far away,

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:53.720
there was a black poster paint.

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:58.150
“White and vermillion 
are always used a lot,

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:03.870
but little black me just 
never seems to get used at all.

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:08.070
I know! Then I'll go 
out and find it myself...

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:10.240
Somewhere, there must be a place

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:12.080
that will accept me for who I am--"

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:14.350
Hey, Kisaragi...

00:17:14.350 --> 00:17:15.580
A little longer!

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:17.460
Just wait a little longer!

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:21.120
Hey, do you know where the 
rough pencils or brushes are?

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:23.410
Noda-chan was using a bunch

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:25.200
of different materials 
earlier for her play...

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:27.010
Just like you said. Really...

00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:27.940
Nooo!

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.130
It's too cute! You can't take 
apart something someone made!

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.760
Then what do you suggest,

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:33.870
that I paint without brushes?!

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:35.400
Well, that's...

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.570
So you went with "Stamping."

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:44.140
 Stamping

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:42.500
Yes!

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:45.430
<b>Also known as "pressure art".</b>

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:47.140
<b>Stamping</b>

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:47.140
<b>A type of modern art which 
makes use of stamps or shapes.</b>

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:49.440
Looks complete for the time being.

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:52.210
When you look at it from here it 
actually looks kinda artistic!

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:55.780
If there's nothing else to add, 
let's submit it like this.

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:56.790
Yeah, of cou-

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:07.060
 Action Painting

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.710
You changed your style?

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.060
Sort of...

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:10.070
<b>Action Painting</b>

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:10.070
<b>A technique that involves 
dripping or splattering paint.</b>

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:12.870
"Kisaragi-chan, Kisaragi-chan,"

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:14.860
said the poster paint.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.180
Oh look, it's Black-poster-paint-san

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:20.110
"Hey hey, use me as well!"

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:22.970
"I refuse!"

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:25.320
responded Tomokane.

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:27.370
No matter how long you

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:28.850
let the black poster paint dry,

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:31.960
it drips and mixes and 
sticks to your fingers!!

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:34.560
It's a menace to other 
colors as well so...

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:34.560
 Mr. Black 
is a little...

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:34.560
Right?

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:36.180
I won't use it!

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:37.790
That's so cruel!

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:42.560
"If only I wasn't black 
and water soluble!"

00:18:43.110 --> 00:18:45.620
Tragically, the black 
poster paint's journey

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.540
was only just beginning.

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:49.430
What's up with that play?

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:50.610
She seems to be having fun.

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:54.110
Now all that's left is to let it dry.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.460
So 'til then let's take a break!

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.120
You've been on break this whole time.

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:01.120
I'll get some drinks from 
the university building.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:02.280
Coffee, please.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.620
I'll come with.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.620
I'll have a coffee, too!

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:05.620
<b>Katou 

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:05.710
Katou or Mutou?

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:05.620
<b>Mutou 

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:07.120
<b>Katou?</b>

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:08.130
<b>Katou?             Mutou?</b>

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:09.130
Noda and Tomo think Katou 
and Mutou are last names.

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:09.940
I'll have Saitou!

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:10.630
<b>Saitou</b>

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:11.630
Then I'll have Itou!

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:11.640
<b>Saitou             Itou</b>

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:17.010
Oh! I completely forgot about sugar.

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:19.480
Kisaragi-dono, you're having black tea?

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:21.370
Here, I brought your coffee.

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:24.370
It's not sugar, but how about this?

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:26.380
Is that jam?

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:28.970
Just as you ordered.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:32.940
I see, Russian tea, right?

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:36.390
By the way, you seem 
to have plenty of jam.

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:38.850
Hey Namiko-san, this coffee tastes weird!

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:41.160
 Saitou (Sugar Disaster)

00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:41.160
I wonder what this gunk at the bottom 
of my cup could be?!

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:41.160
 Itou (Strange Sugar)

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.410
Whoa, no!

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:46.830
Did something happen?

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:50.000
I nearly drank from my paint brush cup.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:52.010
If I hadn't put my brush in it...

00:19:52.010 --> 00:19:53.140
I see.

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:55.770
Even at home, I'll mix 
them up all the time.

00:19:56.140 --> 00:19:57.940
Dangerous, dangerous.

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:01.320
When you're painting, your mind 
is often focused elsewhere.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:05.050
Maybe I should switch to 
a water bottle instead.

00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:10.140
Well, it certainly turned out 
different than we expected.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:11.100
Don't worry.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:13.390
Almost anything can be considered art.

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:16.220
I moved all the tools 
over here, just in case!

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:18.660
Nice work! 
All right, then let's take-

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:18.660
Riiiip!

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:24.970
What's that? That looks fun!

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:27.860
 Collage

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.510
<b>A modern technique where 
pictures, colored paper,</b>

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:30.870
<b> Collage</b>

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:30.870
<b>and cloth are arranged 
and pasted together.</b>

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:34.430
Allll rriiightt!

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:36.440
It sure was a journey!

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:37.690
Just in time, too.

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:39.620
Hurry up and let's go turn it in.

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:43.620
We'll start cleaning up.

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:44.750
Okay!

00:20:44.750 --> 00:20:47.120
Once we drop it off at the staff 
room, we'll come right back.

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:02.000
Kisaragi-chan,

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:04.140
Kisaragi-chan.

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:06.880
<b>A few days later</b>

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.510
Our assignments are back.

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:12.620
Really?

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:15.620
Yamaguchi
Tomokane

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:15.620
"... elaborate production."

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.620
An A!

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:18.130
"An exceptionally elaborate production."

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:19.260
Seriously?

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:22.690
This is the first time I've 
ever gotten a grade this high!

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:24.480
Me too, me too!

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.060
What about us?

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:30.500
Nozaki 
 Oomichi

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:30.500
"... work with a peculiar smell."

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:29.620
B

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:33.360
"A piece of work with a peculiar smell."

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:34.500
That's what they noticed?

00:21:37.260 --> 00:21:39.730
The little black poster paint thought,

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:42.810
"Even though I didn't get used,

00:21:43.430 --> 00:21:46.660
I'm happy that everyone's 
pieces did so well."

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:53.530
So he thought, from the 
bottom of his heart.

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.770 --> 00:23:29.470
The staff room smells like 
coffee and cigarettes.

00:23:29.470 --> 00:23:32.410
That's probably Sotoma-sensei 
and Sasamoto-sensei, right?

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:34.660
There's also the smell 
of paint and chalk.

00:23:34.660 --> 00:23:36.700
I'm a little sleepy today.

00:23:35.110 --> 00:23:40.060
"Life Art"

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:39.570
Chief, look at this! 
It's my newest piece!
